    "voiceover": [
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v01",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v01.mp3",
        "start_frame": 0,
        "duration_frames": 113,
        "text": "A corporate security team had done everything right.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v02",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v02.mp3",
        "start_frame": 113,
        "duration_frames": 178,
        "text": "Hardened firewalls, complex passwords, and round-the-clock intrusion monitoring.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v03",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v03.mp3",
        "start_frame": 291,
        "duration_frames": 182,
        "text": "And yet, an unauthorized intruder still walked away with proprietary source code.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v04",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v04.mp3",
        "start_frame": 473,
        "duration_frames": 200,
        "text": "The strange part was that the attacker never wrote an exploit to breach their defenses.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v05",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v05.mp3",
        "start_frame": 673,
        "duration_frames": 108,
        "text": "He didn't attack the machine. He simply picked up a telephone.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v06",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v06.mp3",
        "start_frame": 781,
        "duration_frames": 156,
        "text": "This is the story of Kevin Mitnick and the revolution of social engineering.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v07",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v07.mp3",
        "start_frame": 937,
        "duration_frames": 224,
        "text": "While security engineers spent millions fortifying software, Mitnick discovered an uncomfortable truth.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v08",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v08.mp3",
        "start_frame": 1161,
        "duration_frames": 242,
        "text": "Computers execute logic deterministically, but humans are driven by trust, urgency, and helpfulness.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v09",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v09.mp3",
        "start_frame": 1403,
        "duration_frames": 192,
        "text": "An attacker with the right pretext could convince an employee to hand over the keys voluntarily.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v10",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v10.mp3",
        "start_frame": 1595,
        "duration_frames": 160,
        "text": "Mitnick's methodology relied on a disciplined four-step cascading loop.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v11",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v11.mp3",
        "start_frame": 1755,
        "duration_frames": 198,
        "text": "First came information gathering: learning internal jargon, employee names, and department codes.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v12",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v12.mp3",
        "start_frame": 1953,
        "duration_frames": 236,
        "text": "Next came pretexting: calling a target under the guise of an IT engineer facing an urgent deadline.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v13",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v13.mp3",
        "start_frame": 2189,
        "duration_frames": 220,
        "text": "By projecting calm authority and manufacturing time pressure, he bypassed critical suspicion.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v14",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v14.mp3",
        "start_frame": 2409,
        "duration_frames": 236,
        "text": "Once inside one department, he leveraged that initial credential to escalate access across the enterprise.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v15",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v15.mp3",
        "start_frame": 2645,
        "duration_frames": 200,
        "text": "Using nothing more than a telephone and social engineering, he compromised telecommunications titans.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v16",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v16.mp3",
        "start_frame": 2845,
        "duration_frames": 194,
        "text": "At Motorola, he obtained the core microcode for next-generation wireless communications.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v17",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v17.mp3",
        "start_frame": 3039,
        "duration_frames": 174,
        "text": "At Digital Equipment Corporation, he acquired the crown-jewel operating system source code.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v18",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v18.mp3",
        "start_frame": 3213,
        "duration_frames": 187,
        "text": "By the early nineteen-nineties, Mitnick was the most wanted cyber fugitive in American history.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v19",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v19.mp3",
        "start_frame": 3400,
        "duration_frames": 241,
        "text": "On February fifteenth, nineteen ninety-five, federal agents raided his apartment in Raleigh, North Carolina.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v20",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v20.mp3",
        "start_frame": 3641,
        "duration_frames": 230,
        "text": "His capture triggered intense national debate over the boundaries of digital defense and human psychology.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v21",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v21.mp3",
        "start_frame": 3871,
        "duration_frames": 213,
        "text": "After serving five years in prison, Mitnick redirected his expertise toward defensive security.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v22",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v22.mp3",
        "start_frame": 4084,
        "duration_frames": 216,
        "text": "His seminal work, The Art of Deception, transformed enterprise security training forever.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v23",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v23.mp3",
        "start_frame": 4300,
        "duration_frames": 221,
        "text": "Today, multi-factor authentication and zero-trust architectures exist because of these hard-learned lessons.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      },
      {
        "clip_id": "vox_v24",
        "file": "audio/v02_sentences/v24.mp3",
        "start_frame": 4521,
        "duration_frames": 237,
        "text": "The greatest lesson of Kevin Mitnick remains clear: the password was never the real target\u2014trust was.",
        "speaker": "Narrator (Andrew)"
      }
    ],
